{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1793036995,"nonce":"4anhok5x8f6zBV5iDwXtfpTp+84=","message":"Completed in ef848bb08b4c26b12d7189465466e09145b1e14c.\n\nHosted filesystem writes, moves, deletes and directory creation now enter the bounded recovery FIFO. A durable intent precedes compute execution and its result precedes the public acknowledgement. Applied mutations invalidate older matching document heads; pending or uncertain operations continue blocking matching heads until future reconciliation. Refused preconditions preserve the earlier head. Path-prefix matching covers rename destinations and directory descendants without affecting neighbouring names.\n\nOnly native-confirmed Save/journal barriers promote restore heads atomically with their payload. Historical imports cannot promote a head; a changed selected payload invalidates its stamp, including deletion-only CRDT changes with unchanged vectors. The private owner-checked restore catalog is source-scoped, revision-fenced, and explicitly reports automaticRestore:false. It is document selection, not a complete filesystem snapshot. The head index is separate from the small counters so each edit does not rewrite the whole index.\n\nNative direct writes update an open CRDT document before acknowledgement. Shared files and containing directories must be released before delete/rename; host-local symlink and case aliases are checked. This does not establish stable canonical document identities across machines.\n\nValidation: 49 native tests, 14 Rust Worker integration tests and 38 browser-session tests passed; core-only native check and builds passed. Both full-WASM editor flows passed (collaboration and hosted GitHub sign-in/edit/durable Save/reload). Coverage includes compute loss during a write, object restart, same-content barriers, unchanged-vector imported deletions, owner/source isolation, stale catalog revisions, alias guards, mutation/metadata quotas and filesystem queue admission before side effects. The final Worker-only counter/index optimization passed the Worker suite and hosted browser flow again.\n\nLimits are prototype guards: 1,024 mutations, 512 document heads, 1 MiB catalog metadata, 256 queued recovery operations and 16 MiB queued encoded filesystem payload. File bodies are not stored in the mutation ledger. Full filesystem state, external-change reconciliation, stable identities, catalog materialization, compute leases/fencing and production MSB provisioning remain open under the parent tracks. WASM/native session rebuilt, tested bundle staged at bin/web/rayde and local service restarted and checked. No push or deployment.","files":null}]}